1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,999
ⓘ These English & Foreign subtitles created by ZoowlCZ (ver. 2024-10) are an expanded version of the English subtitles created by Bokutox of YIFY-TORRENTS (Torporr of Outland PVP (EU)).

2
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,951
You may go no further.

3
00:00:21,387 --> 00:00:23,888
You will not enter Gondor.

4
00:00:24,513 --> 00:00:26,931
Who are you to deny us passage?

5
00:00:27,014 --> 00:00:30,973
Legolas, fire a warning shot past the bosun's ear.

6
00:00:32,744 --> 00:00:34,307
Mind your aim.

7
00:00:41,035 --> 00:00:43,578
That's it. Right. We warned you.

8
00:00:43,786 --> 00:00:45,766
Prepare to be boarded.

9
00:00:47,537 --> 00:00:48,672
Boarded?

10
00:00:48,683 --> 00:00:50,663
By you and whose army?

11
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,891
This army.

12
00:01:11,081 --> 00:01:12,539
In there.

13
00:01:14,623 --> 00:01:16,342
What is this place?

14
00:01:20,873 --> 00:01:24,154
Master must go inside the tunnel.

15
00:01:25,822 --> 00:01:29,312
Now that I'm here, I don't think I want to.

16
00:01:31,968 --> 00:01:33,688
It's the only way.

17
00:01:36,292 --> 00:01:38,062
Go in...

18
00:01:38,542 --> 00:01:40,746
or go back.

19
00:01:43,584 --> 00:01:46,203
I can't go back.

20
00:01:59,002 --> 00:02:01,544
- What's that smell?
- Orcses' filth.

21
00:02:01,555 --> 00:02:04,500
Orcses come in here sometimes.

22
00:02:10,097 --> 00:02:11,347
Hurry.

23
00:02:16,608 --> 00:02:18,171
This way.

24
00:02:21,191 --> 00:02:22,806
Smeagol?

25
00:02:23,952 --> 00:02:25,931
Over here.

26
00:02:35,047 --> 00:02:37,391
It's sticky. What is it?

27
00:02:38,172 --> 00:02:39,891
You will see.

28
00:02:40,465 --> 00:02:42,340
Oh, yes.

29
00:02:42,809 --> 00:02:45,670
You will see.

30
00:02:54,945 --> 00:02:56,508
Smeagol?

31
00:02:58,279 --> 00:02:59,303
Smeagol!

32
00:03:01,925 --> 00:03:03,593
Smeagol!

33
00:03:13,176 --> 00:03:14,632
Sam.

34
00:04:55,009 --> 00:04:57,323
And you, Frodo Baggins...

35
00:04:57,333 --> 00:05:02,265
I give you the light of
Earendil, our most beloved star.

36
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,719
May it be a light for you in dark places...

37
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,847
when all other lights go out.

38
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:13,822
[Quenya] <i>Aiya Eärendil, Elenion Ancalima!</i>
[English] Hail Eärendil, Brightest of the Stars!

39
00:06:26,789 --> 00:06:29,604
Naughty little fly.

40
00:06:30,227 --> 00:06:33,561
Why does he cry?

41
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:37,155
Caught in a web

42
00:06:37,571 --> 00:06:39,780
Soon you'll be...

43
00:06:40,155 --> 00:06:41,981
Eaten.

44
00:07:20,076 --> 00:07:21,992
Got away, did it, precious?

45
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:24,191
Not this time.

46
00:07:24,399 --> 00:07:27,366
- Not this time!
- No!

47
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:37,533
It wasn't us. It wasn't us!

48
00:07:38,463 --> 00:07:41,016
Smeagol wouldn't hurt master.

49
00:07:41,172 --> 00:07:42,694
We promised.

50
00:07:43,151 --> 00:07:45,598
You must believe us.

51
00:07:45,703 --> 00:07:47,243
It was the precious.

52
00:07:48,047 --> 00:07:52,200
The precious made us do it.

53
00:08:09,612 --> 00:08:12,205
I have to destroy it, Smeagol.

54
00:08:21,644 --> 00:08:24,538
I have to destroy it for both our sakes.

55
00:08:34,979 --> 00:08:36,035
No!

56
00:08:59,565 --> 00:09:01,658
I'm so sorry, Sam.

57
00:09:06,545 --> 00:09:08,699
I'm so sorry.

58
00:09:34,985 --> 00:09:39,246
This task was appointed to you, Frodo of the Shire.

59
00:09:40,767 --> 00:09:42,903
If you do not find a way...

60
00:09:44,413 --> 00:09:46,028
no one will.

61
00:10:19,729 --> 00:10:21,843
The scouts report Minas Tirith is surrounded.

62
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:24,298
The lower level's in flames.

63
00:10:25,042 --> 00:10:27,214
Everywhere, legions of the enemy advance.

64
00:10:28,012 --> 00:10:29,209
Time is against us.

65
00:10:29,261 --> 00:10:30,505
Make ready!

66
00:10:30,771 --> 00:10:32,503
Take heart, Merry.

67
00:10:32,856 --> 00:10:34,887
It will soon be over.

68
00:10:35,949 --> 00:10:37,179
My lady...

69
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:40,305
you are fair and brave...

70
00:10:40,825 --> 00:10:43,065
and have much to live for...

71
00:10:44,679 --> 00:10:46,709
and many who love you.

72
00:10:49,889 --> 00:10:52,221
I know it is too late to turn aside.

73
00:10:53,379 --> 00:10:55,964
I know there is not much point now in hoping.

74
00:10:57,338 --> 00:11:00,931
If I were a knight of Rohan, capable of great deeds...

75
00:11:00,932 --> 00:11:03,881
But
- I'm not.

76
00:11:04,317 --> 00:11:05,890
I'm a Hobbit.

77
00:11:09,036 --> 00:11:11,100
And I know I can't save Middle-earth.

78
00:11:14,891 --> 00:11:16,797
I just want to help my friends.

79
00:11:19,214 --> 00:11:20,384
Frodo.

80
00:11:21,715 --> 00:11:22,973
Sam.

81
00:11:25,048 --> 00:11:26,597
Pippin.

82
00:11:28,382 --> 00:11:31,611
More than anything, I wish I could see them again.

83
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:37,633
Prepare to move out!

84
00:11:38,008 --> 00:11:41,248
Make haste. We ride through the night.

85
00:11:57,655 --> 00:11:58,645
To battle.

86
00:11:59,322 --> 00:12:00,624
To battle.

87
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:25,271
Back to the gate!

88
00:12:25,992 --> 00:12:27,720
Hurry!

89
00:12:47,869 --> 00:12:52,101
I am steward of the House of Anarion.

90
00:12:52,557 --> 00:12:54,745
Thus have I walked.

91
00:12:56,203 --> 00:12:59,120
And thus now will I sleep.

92
00:13:05,319 --> 00:13:07,107
Gondor is lost.

93
00:13:07,819 --> 00:13:11,017
There is no hope for Men.

94
00:13:26,154 --> 00:13:28,444
Why do the fools fly?

95
00:13:30,373 --> 00:13:33,070
Better to die sooner than late.

96
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:37,271
For die we must.

97
00:13:49,907 --> 00:13:53,240
No tomb for Denethor and Faramir.

98
00:13:54,073 --> 00:13:59,595
No long, slow sleep of death embalmed.

99
00:14:00,271 --> 00:14:04,897
We shall burn, like the heathen kings of old.

100
00:14:09,023 --> 00:14:10,400
Bring wood and oil.

101
00:14:13,659 --> 00:14:14,568
Steady.

102
00:14:15,273 --> 00:14:16,780
Steady.

103
00:14:31,629 --> 00:14:33,921
You are soldiers of Gondor.

104
00:14:34,442 --> 00:14:38,765
No matter what comes through that
gate, you will stand your ground.

105
00:14:45,036 --> 00:14:46,036
Run!

106
00:14:48,453 --> 00:14:49,756
Volley!

107
00:14:50,663 --> 00:14:52,076
Fire!

108
00:16:45,653 --> 00:16:47,372
Let him go, you filth.

109
00:16:49,424 --> 00:16:50,810
Let him go!

110
00:16:52,425 --> 00:16:54,507
You will not touch him again.

111
00:16:57,790 --> 00:16:59,248
Come on and finish it.

112
00:18:49,311 --> 00:18:50,434
Back!

113
00:19:01,656 --> 00:19:02,802
Mr. Frodo.

114
00:19:12,594 --> 00:19:14,054
Oh, no.

115
00:19:14,679 --> 00:19:16,185
Frodo.

116
00:19:16,814 --> 00:19:18,353
Mr. Frodo.

117
00:19:23,294 --> 00:19:24,419
Wake up.

118
00:19:28,533 --> 00:19:30,670
Don't leave me here alone.

119
00:19:32,493 --> 00:19:34,628
Don't go where I can't follow.

120
00:19:39,056 --> 00:19:40,202
Wake up.

121
00:19:47,129 --> 00:19:49,057
Not asleep.

122
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,119
Dead.

123
00:20:12,028 --> 00:20:13,903
You get back, you scum!

124
00:20:23,331 --> 00:20:24,894
What's this?

125
00:20:25,748 --> 00:20:28,644
Looks like old Shelob's been having a bit of fun.

126
00:20:30,467 --> 00:20:32,811
Killed another one, has she?

127
00:20:33,124 --> 00:20:34,948
No.

128
00:20:37,863 --> 00:20:39,962
This fellow ain't dead.

129
00:20:39,967 --> 00:20:42,135
Not dead?

130
00:20:42,655 --> 00:20:48,073
- She jabs him with her stinger,
and he goes as limp as a boned fish.

131
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:51,354
Then she has her way with them.

132
00:20:51,927 --> 00:20:53,959
That's how she likes to feed.

133
00:20:54,115 --> 00:20:56,042
Fresh blood.

134
00:20:56,251 --> 00:20:58,438
Get him to the tower!

135
00:21:02,137 --> 00:21:03,887
Samwise, you fool.

136
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:06,773
This scum will be awake in a couple of hours.

137
00:21:07,084 --> 00:21:09,325
Then he'll wish he'd never been born.

138
00:21:33,807 --> 00:21:36,827
The house of his spirit crumbles.

139
00:21:38,182 --> 00:21:39,432
He is burning.

140
00:21:40,734 --> 00:21:42,089
Already burning.

141
00:21:42,454 --> 00:21:44,017
He's not dead.

142
00:21:44,798 --> 00:21:46,361
He's not dead!

143
00:21:48,444 --> 00:21:50,119
No! No!

144
00:21:50,631 --> 00:21:52,611
No! No!

145
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:55,059
He's not dead!

146
00:21:55,579 --> 00:21:58,861
- Farewell, Peregrin, son of Paladin.
- No! No! No!

147
00:21:59,069 --> 00:22:02,196
I release you from my service.

148
00:22:03,550 --> 00:22:07,872
Go now and die in what way seems best to you.

149
00:22:10,227 --> 00:22:12,280
Pour oil on the wood!

150
00:22:14,175 --> 00:22:16,037
Come on, soldier! Move it!

151
00:22:16,780 --> 00:22:19,455
- Hurry along there! Hurry along!
- Gandalf!

152
00:22:20,113 --> 00:22:21,363
Where is Gandalf?

153
00:22:22,822 --> 00:22:23,863
Gandalf!

154
00:22:29,646 --> 00:22:30,688
Retreat!

155
00:22:32,876 --> 00:22:34,594
The city is breached!

156
00:22:34,749 --> 00:22:37,667
Fall back! To the second level!

157
00:22:41,522 --> 00:22:43,292
Get the women and children out!

158
00:22:43,397 --> 00:22:45,064
Get them out!

159
00:22:45,335 --> 00:22:46,679
Retreat!

160
00:22:46,783 --> 00:22:48,763
Come on. Come on, move.

161
00:22:48,971 --> 00:22:53,293
Move into the city. Kill all in your path.

162
00:23:01,368 --> 00:23:03,608
Take them down!

163
00:23:24,390 --> 00:23:27,204
Fight! Fight to the last man!

164
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,871
Fight for your lives!

165
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:30,212
Gandalf!

166
00:23:34,464 --> 00:23:35,641
Gandalf!

167
00:23:35,746 --> 00:23:38,403
Denethor has lost his mind!

168
00:23:38,611 --> 00:23:40,799
He's burning Faramir alive!

169
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:42,778
Up! Quickly!

170
00:23:49,862 --> 00:23:51,060
Go back to the abyss.

171
00:23:52,883 --> 00:23:56,216
Fall into the nothingness that
awaits you and your master.

172
00:23:56,569 --> 00:24:02,885
Do you not know death when you see it, old man?

173
00:24:03,092 --> 00:24:07,125
This is my hour.

174
00:24:17,365 --> 00:24:18,353
Gandalf!

175
00:24:27,595 --> 00:24:30,804
You have failed.

176
00:24:31,866 --> 00:24:36,742
The world of Men will fall.

177
00:25:33,882 --> 00:25:34,975
Courage, Merry.

178
00:25:35,549 --> 00:25:37,633
Courage for our friends.

179
00:25:41,457 --> 00:25:44,583
Form ranks, you maggots. Form ranks!

180
00:25:44,613 --> 00:25:47,790
Pikes in front. Archers behind.

181
00:25:56,020 --> 00:25:59,198
Eomer, take your Eored down the left flank.

182
00:25:59,437 --> 00:26:00,501
Flank ready.

183
00:26:00,969 --> 00:26:03,416
Gamling, follow the king's banner down the center.

184
00:26:03,573 --> 00:26:07,376
Grimbold, take your company
right after you pass the wall.

185
00:26:07,688 --> 00:26:10,085
Forth, and fear no darkness!

186
00:26:10,501 --> 00:26:14,148
Arise, arise, Riders of Theoden!

187
00:26:14,522 --> 00:26:19,668
Spears shall be shaken...
Shields shall be splintered...

188
00:26:19,981 --> 00:26:23,471
a sword-day, a red day...

189
00:26:23,794 --> 00:26:27,145
and the sun rises!

190
00:26:35,190 --> 00:26:39,671
Whatever happens, stay with me. I'll look after you.

191
00:26:45,870 --> 00:26:47,900
Ride now!

192
00:26:49,411 --> 00:26:51,271
Ride now!

193
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:54,932
Ride! Ride for ruin...

194
00:26:55,141 --> 00:26:58,319
and the world's ending!

195
00:26:59,725 --> 00:27:03,631
- Death!
- Death!

196
00:27:04,725 --> 00:27:07,798
- Death!
- Death!

197
00:27:08,569 --> 00:27:10,403
- Death!
- Death!

198
00:27:10,820 --> 00:27:15,091
- Death!
- Death!

199
00:27:19,206 --> 00:27:21,706
For Eorlingas!

200
00:28:04,783 --> 00:28:06,086
Fire!

201
00:28:10,304 --> 00:28:12,128
Death!

202
00:28:15,669 --> 00:28:17,389
Charge!

203
00:28:17,441 --> 00:28:18,527
Fire at will!

204
00:29:16,457 --> 00:29:19,321
Set a fire in our flesh.

205
00:29:37,209 --> 00:29:38,856
Stay this madness!

206
00:29:43,273 --> 00:29:47,606
You may triumph in the field of battle for a day...

207
00:29:48,241 --> 00:29:51,773
but against the power that has risen in the east...

208
00:29:52,138 --> 00:29:55,003
there is no victory.

209
00:30:24,537 --> 00:30:26,204
No!

210
00:30:26,266 --> 00:30:29,120
You will not take my son from me!

211
00:30:29,151 --> 00:30:31,256
No!

212
00:30:42,456 --> 00:30:43,861
Faramir.

213
00:30:57,666 --> 00:31:01,363
So passes Denethor, son of Ecthelion.

214
00:31:29,282 --> 00:31:31,366
Drive them to the river!

215
00:31:33,710 --> 00:31:36,003
Make safe the city!

216
00:32:15,745 --> 00:32:17,464
Re-form the line!

217
00:32:18,663 --> 00:32:20,538
Re-form the line!

218
00:32:27,726 --> 00:32:30,486
Sound the charge! Take them head-on!

219
00:32:30,955 --> 00:32:33,143
Charge!

220
00:33:51,901 --> 00:33:53,151
Cut him down!

221
00:34:20,134 --> 00:34:22,582
Take the reins. Pull him left!

222
00:34:24,978 --> 00:34:26,071
Left!

223
00:34:43,833 --> 00:34:45,292
Aim for their heads!

224
00:34:51,334 --> 00:34:54,669
Bring it down! Bring it down! Bring it down!

225
00:35:00,345 --> 00:35:01,283
Merry!

226
00:35:08,523 --> 00:35:09,929
Merry!

227
00:36:23,323 --> 00:36:25,249
I didn't think it would end this way.

228
00:36:26,604 --> 00:36:28,062
End?

229
00:36:29,438 --> 00:36:31,657
No, the journey doesn't end here.

230
00:36:33,938 --> 00:36:36,866
Death is just another path...

231
00:36:37,731 --> 00:36:39,730
one that we all must take.

232
00:36:40,699 --> 00:36:44,262
The grey rain curtain of this world rolls back...

233
00:36:44,366 --> 00:36:47,804
and all turns to silver glass.

234
00:36:50,096 --> 00:36:51,868
And then you see it.

235
00:36:53,783 --> 00:36:56,294
What, Gandalf?

236
00:36:57,461 --> 00:36:58,899
See what?

237
00:37:00,019 --> 00:37:02,024
White shores...

238
00:37:03,900 --> 00:37:06,140
and beyond.

239
00:37:07,703 --> 00:37:09,576
A far green country...

240
00:37:10,338 --> 00:37:13,066
under a swift sunrise.

241
00:37:17,234 --> 00:37:18,954
Well...

242
00:37:19,006 --> 00:37:20,568
that isn't so bad.

243
00:37:20,589 --> 00:37:21,870
No.

244
00:37:24,213 --> 00:37:25,828
No, it isn't.

245
00:37:42,132 --> 00:37:45,518
Rally to me! To me!

246
00:38:06,458 --> 00:38:10,833
Feast on his flesh.

247
00:38:15,261 --> 00:38:17,396
I will kill you if you touch him.

248
00:38:17,407 --> 00:38:22,918
Do not come between the Nazgul and his prey.

249
00:39:31,831 --> 00:39:35,217
Late as usual, pirate scum!

250
00:39:35,451 --> 00:39:37,248
There's knife-work here needs doing.

251
00:39:37,299 --> 00:39:41,115
Come on, you sea rats! Get off your ships!

252
00:39:56,234 --> 00:39:58,608
There's plenty for the both of us.

253
00:39:58,708 --> 00:40:01,052
May the best Dwarf win.

254
00:40:18,398 --> 00:40:20,622
You fool.

255
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:24,206
No man can kill me.

256
00:40:26,576 --> 00:40:29,750
Die now.

257
00:40:40,379 --> 00:40:42,412
I am no man.

258
00:40:58,923 --> 00:41:02,419
- 15! 16!
- 17!

259
00:41:10,215 --> 00:41:12,124
Merry!

260
00:41:54,095 --> 00:41:55,885
Legolas!

261
00:42:18,265 --> 00:42:20,634
33, 34.

262
00:43:07,686 --> 00:43:10,056
That still only counts as one!

263
00:43:10,186 --> 00:43:12,384
Come on, then. Come on!

264
00:43:56,066 --> 00:43:58,898
I know your face...

265
00:44:00,681 --> 00:44:02,600
Eowyn.

266
00:44:05,191 --> 00:44:07,561
My eyes darken.

267
00:44:08,651 --> 00:44:10,087
No.

268
00:44:10,901 --> 00:44:12,588
No.

269
00:44:14,594 --> 00:44:17,099
I am going to save you.

270
00:44:18,422 --> 00:44:20,766
You already did.

271
00:44:24,444 --> 00:44:26,066
Eowyn...

272
00:44:27,517 --> 00:44:30,058
my body is broken.

273
00:44:35,064 --> 00:44:37,564
You have to let me go.

274
00:44:43,424 --> 00:44:46,017
I go to my fathers...

275
00:44:47,466 --> 00:44:50,320
in whose mighty company...

276
00:44:50,737 --> 00:44:54,110
I shall not now feel ashamed.

277
00:45:10,667 --> 00:45:12,321
Eowyn.

278
00:45:58,745 --> 00:46:01,240
Release us.

279
00:46:03,094 --> 00:46:04,867
Bad idea.

280
00:46:05,021 --> 00:46:08,745
Very handy in a tight spot, these
lads, despite the fact they're dead.

281
00:46:08,771 --> 00:46:11,028
You gave us your word.

282
00:46:12,704 --> 00:46:14,892
I hold your oath fulfilled.

283
00:46:16,115 --> 00:46:17,573
Go.

284
00:46:18,277 --> 00:46:20,113
Be at peace.

285
00:47:03,376 --> 00:47:05,313
Merry.

286
00:47:05,887 --> 00:47:09,220
No!

287
00:47:12,762 --> 00:47:15,522
No!

288
00:47:39,151 --> 00:47:43,078
With a sigh.

289
00:47:43,193 --> 00:47:46,952
You turn away.

290
00:47:47,088 --> 00:47:51,120
With a deepening heart.

291
00:47:51,151 --> 00:47:56,048
No more words to say.

292
00:47:56,173 --> 00:47:59,694
You will find.

293
00:47:59,745 --> 00:48:08,236
That the world has changed forever.

294
00:48:32,905 --> 00:48:40,709
And the trees are now turning from green to gold.

295
00:48:44,573 --> 00:48:49,386
And the sun is now fading.

296
00:48:49,491 --> 00:48:59,554
I wish I could hold you closer.

297
00:49:02,382 --> 00:49:03,658
Merry!

298
00:49:05,200 --> 00:49:07,305
Merry!

299
00:49:18,639 --> 00:49:20,465
Merry.

300
00:49:22,932 --> 00:49:24,176
Merry, it's me.

301
00:49:26,787 --> 00:49:28,348
It's Pippin.

302
00:49:30,848 --> 00:49:33,135
I knew you'd find me.

303
00:49:33,307 --> 00:49:34,504
Yes.

304
00:49:36,933 --> 00:49:39,008
Are you going to leave me?

305
00:49:39,558 --> 00:49:41,265
No, Merry.

306
00:49:42,559 --> 00:49:44,798
I'm going to look after you.

307
00:50:28,459 --> 00:50:30,180
Hands off!

308
00:50:30,334 --> 00:50:33,519
That shiny shirt, that's mine.

309
00:50:33,771 --> 00:50:37,932
It's going to the Great Eye,
along with everything else.

310
00:50:39,450 --> 00:50:43,356
I don't take orders from stinking Morgul-rats!

311
00:50:44,137 --> 00:50:49,294
You touch it, and I'll stick this blade in your gut.

312
00:51:09,765 --> 00:51:11,693
The scum tried to knife me.

313
00:51:11,745 --> 00:51:13,684
Kill him!

314
00:52:56,754 --> 00:52:58,819
That's for Frodo!

315
00:52:59,099 --> 00:53:01,324
And for the Shire!

316
00:53:04,725 --> 00:53:07,033
And that's for my old Gaffer!

317
00:53:36,446 --> 00:53:39,829
Stop your squealing, you dunghill rat.

318
00:53:40,926 --> 00:53:45,662
I'm gonna bleed you like a stuck pig.

319
00:53:52,907 --> 00:53:54,659
Not if I stick you first.

320
00:53:54,782 --> 00:53:56,344
Sam!

321
00:54:01,397 --> 00:54:03,480
Oh, Sam, I'm so sorry.

322
00:54:03,532 --> 00:54:05,664
Sorry for everything.

323
00:54:05,876 --> 00:54:09,830
- Let's get you out of here.
- It's too late. It's over.

324
00:54:09,940 --> 00:54:12,870
They've taken it. Sam...

325
00:54:13,637 --> 00:54:15,162
they took the Ring.

326
00:54:15,877 --> 00:54:18,621
Begging your pardon, but they haven't.

327
00:54:30,566 --> 00:54:32,792
I thought I'd lost you.

328
00:54:33,171 --> 00:54:34,877
So I took it.

329
00:54:36,036 --> 00:54:38,120
Only for safekeeping.

330
00:54:39,370 --> 00:54:41,121
Give it to me.

331
00:54:44,630 --> 00:54:46,876
Give me the Ring, Sam.

332
00:54:51,506 --> 00:54:52,791
Sam.

333
00:54:54,371 --> 00:54:56,336
Give me the Ring.

334
00:55:17,030 --> 00:55:18,330
You must understand.

335
00:55:21,822 --> 00:55:23,668
The Ring is my burden.

336
00:55:24,842 --> 00:55:26,999
It will destroy you, Sam.

337
00:55:30,155 --> 00:55:32,131
Come on, Mr. Frodo.

338
00:55:33,437 --> 00:55:35,092
We best find you some clothes.

339
00:55:35,261 --> 00:55:38,294
You can't go walking through
Mordor in naught but your skin.

340
00:56:00,013 --> 00:56:02,217
We did it, Mr. Frodo.

341
00:56:02,722 --> 00:56:05,008
We made it to Mordor.

342
00:56:06,347 --> 00:56:08,005
There are so many of them.

343
00:56:08,972 --> 00:56:11,542
We'll never get through unseen.

344
00:56:16,670 --> 00:56:20,012
It's him, the Eye.

345
00:56:27,723 --> 00:56:30,343
We have to go in there, Mr. Frodo.

346
00:56:30,808 --> 00:56:32,845
There's nothing for it.

347
00:56:35,850 --> 00:56:40,258
Come on. Let's just make it down the hill for starters.

348
00:56:49,435 --> 00:56:52,849
Frodo has passed beyond my sight.

349
00:56:54,122 --> 00:56:56,987
The darkness is deepening.

350
00:56:57,039 --> 00:56:59,331
If Sauron had the Ring, we would know it.

351
00:56:59,342 --> 00:57:01,765
It's only a matter of time.

352
00:57:03,238 --> 00:57:05,675
He has suffered a defeat, yes but...

353
00:57:06,728 --> 00:57:11,207
behind the walls of Mordor, our enemy is regrouping.

354
00:57:11,363 --> 00:57:13,135
Let him stay there.

355
00:57:13,145 --> 00:57:16,020
Let him rot! Why should we care?

356
00:57:16,083 --> 00:57:21,417
Because 10,000 Orcs now stand
between Frodo and Mount Doom.

357
00:57:28,083 --> 00:57:30,635
I've sent him to his death.

358
00:57:32,147 --> 00:57:33,468
No.

359
00:57:33,971 --> 00:57:36,387
There is still hope for Frodo.

360
00:57:36,731 --> 00:57:40,855
He needs time and safe passage
across the plains of Gorgoroth.

361
00:57:41,939 --> 00:57:44,510
- We can give him that.
- How?

362
00:57:44,857 --> 00:57:47,559
Draw out Sauron's armies.

363
00:57:47,722 --> 00:57:49,853
Empty his lands.

364
00:57:50,066 --> 00:57:53,146
Then we gather our full strength
and march on the Black Gate.

365
00:57:53,711 --> 00:57:56,772
We cannot achieve victory through strength of arms.

366
00:57:56,941 --> 00:57:58,517
Not for ourselves.

367
00:57:58,712 --> 00:58:04,315
But we can give Frodo his chance if
we keep Sauron's Eye fixed upon us.

368
00:58:06,109 --> 00:58:09,889
Keep him blind to all else that moves.

369
00:58:10,640 --> 00:58:11,848
A diversion.

370
00:58:11,995 --> 00:58:13,815
Certainty of death...

371
00:58:13,922 --> 00:58:16,734
small chance of success...

372
00:58:17,568 --> 00:58:19,186
what are we waiting for?

373
00:58:19,757 --> 00:58:22,182
Sauron will suspect a trap.

374
00:58:22,985 --> 00:58:25,022
He will not take the bait.

375
00:58:26,527 --> 00:58:29,016
Oh, I think he will.

376
00:59:03,302 --> 00:59:06,011
Long have you hunted me.

377
00:59:06,218 --> 00:59:08,197
Long have I eluded you.

378
00:59:09,813 --> 00:59:11,608
No more.

379
00:59:13,251 --> 00:59:15,729
Behold the Sword of Elendil.

380
01:00:00,182 --> 01:00:02,692
The city has fallen silent.

381
01:00:04,350 --> 01:00:07,403
There is no warmth left in the sun.

382
01:00:08,204 --> 01:00:09,910
It grows so cold.

383
01:00:12,892 --> 01:00:15,946
It's just the damp of the first spring rain.

384
01:00:22,320 --> 01:00:25,531
I do not believe this darkness will endure.

385
01:00:54,093 --> 01:00:55,708
Look, the Orcs...

386
01:00:56,178 --> 01:00:58,241
they're moving off.

387
01:00:59,292 --> 01:01:01,367
You see, Mr. Frodo...

388
01:01:01,543 --> 01:01:03,867
some luck at last.

389
01:01:04,043 --> 01:01:05,868
Move it, you slugs!

390
01:01:07,116 --> 01:01:10,534
Come on! Faster!

391
01:01:18,420 --> 01:01:21,648
Come along, you coldhearted wretched scum...

392
01:01:21,659 --> 01:01:26,204
I'll whip you down to the bone, you...

393
01:01:29,046 --> 01:01:30,713
Come on!

394
01:01:30,880 --> 01:01:33,089
What have I told you?

395
01:01:33,109 --> 01:01:35,400
No evation...

396
01:01:36,389 --> 01:01:38,213
Now move it!

397
01:01:40,036 --> 01:01:41,539
Get up!

398
01:01:41,912 --> 01:01:44,589
Come on, you slugs!

399
01:01:44,724 --> 01:01:48,370
You two are going straight to the front line!

400
01:01:48,548 --> 01:01:53,839
Now, move it! Go on! Fall
in! Move it! Move it! Move it!

401
01:02:06,393 --> 01:02:10,196
To the Gate, you slugs! Now, move it!

402
01:02:19,623 --> 01:02:23,213
Don't you know we're at war?

403
01:02:45,512 --> 01:02:48,379
Company, halt!

404
01:02:52,179 --> 01:02:55,586
Inspection!

405
01:02:55,721 --> 01:02:58,216
Sam, help me.

406
01:02:58,378 --> 01:03:00,213
Mr. Frodo!

407
01:03:02,909 --> 01:03:05,465
Stand up, Mr. Frodo. Stand up!

408
01:03:05,617 --> 01:03:07,463
It's so heavy.

409
01:03:16,557 --> 01:03:17,760
Oh, no.

410
01:03:23,379 --> 01:03:25,381
What do I do? What do we do?

411
01:03:28,432 --> 01:03:29,594
- Hit me.
- What?

412
01:03:29,735 --> 01:03:31,804
Hit me, Sam. Start fighting.

413
01:03:31,974 --> 01:03:33,550
Get off of me!

414
01:03:34,214 --> 01:03:36,548
Nobody pushes me, you filthy maggot.

415
01:03:45,153 --> 01:03:47,222
Get off of me!

416
01:03:48,121 --> 01:03:50,050
Break it up! Break it up!

417
01:03:52,602 --> 01:03:57,218
Oi! I'll have your guts if you
don't shut this rabble down!

418
01:03:57,238 --> 01:03:59,675
Go, Sam. Now!

419
01:04:08,593 --> 01:04:10,144
Move along, scum!

420
01:04:10,311 --> 01:04:12,219
Back in the line!

421
01:04:12,707 --> 01:04:14,519
You maggots!

422
01:04:15,156 --> 01:04:18,185
Get back into the line, you slugs!

423
01:04:20,521 --> 01:04:24,052
Dig it, you slugs. Move it.

424
01:05:12,714 --> 01:05:14,856
I can't...

425
01:05:15,006 --> 01:05:18,771
I can't... I can't manage the Ring, Sam.

426
01:05:18,860 --> 01:05:20,099
It's... It's...

427
01:05:20,267 --> 01:05:22,848
It's such a weight to carry.

428
01:05:23,704 --> 01:05:24,766
It's...

429
01:05:24,903 --> 01:05:26,899
Such a weight.

430
01:05:31,829 --> 01:05:34,330
We're going that way. Straight as we can.

431
01:05:35,684 --> 01:05:38,915
There's no point carrying
anything we're not sure to need.

432
01:05:53,967 --> 01:05:55,897
Mr. Frodo.

433
01:05:57,354 --> 01:05:58,898
Look.

434
01:06:01,364 --> 01:06:03,314
There is light...

435
01:06:03,656 --> 01:06:05,218
and beauty up there...

436
01:06:05,479 --> 01:06:07,946
that no shadow can touch.

437
01:06:58,923 --> 01:07:00,576
Take mine.

438
01:07:01,057 --> 01:07:03,199
There's a few drops left.

439
01:07:18,351 --> 01:07:20,985
There will be none left for the return journey.

440
01:07:21,893 --> 01:07:25,078
I don't think there will be
a return journey, Mr. Frodo.

441
01:07:59,570 --> 01:08:01,568
[Black Speech] <i> Kelkum-ishi. </i>
[English]  In the coldness.

442
01:08:17,888 --> 01:08:20,076
Frodo, get down!

443
01:08:21,795 --> 01:08:23,744
Hide!

444
01:08:33,880 --> 01:08:35,917
Frodo!

445
01:08:41,693 --> 01:08:43,165
Where are they?

446
01:09:19,196 --> 01:09:22,252
Let the Lord of the Black Land come forth!

447
01:09:23,156 --> 01:09:26,009
Let justice be done upon him!

448
01:10:09,410 --> 01:10:13,418
My master, Sauron the Great, bids thee welcome.

449
01:10:19,254 --> 01:10:22,962
Is there any in this rout with
authority to treat with me?

450
01:10:23,318 --> 01:10:26,466
We do not come to treat with Sauron...

451
01:10:26,599 --> 01:10:29,151
faithless and accursed.

452
01:10:29,161 --> 01:10:33,162
Tell your master this: The
armies of Mordor must disband.

453
01:10:33,266 --> 01:10:36,080
He is to depart these lands, never to return.

454
01:10:37,017 --> 01:10:39,595
Old Greybeard.

455
01:10:40,924 --> 01:10:45,307
I have a token I was bidden to show thee.

456
01:10:50,310 --> 01:10:51,637
Frodo.

457
01:10:54,477 --> 01:10:55,935
Frodo.

458
01:10:56,655 --> 01:10:58,132
- Silence.
- No!

459
01:10:58,737 --> 01:11:00,304
Silence!

460
01:11:02,072 --> 01:11:05,848
The Halfling was dear to thee, I see.

461
01:11:06,760 --> 01:11:10,930
Know that he suffered greatly at the hands of his host.

462
01:11:16,291 --> 01:11:22,186
Who would've thought one so
small could endure so much pain?

463
01:11:24,782 --> 01:11:26,933
And he did, Gandalf.

464
01:11:27,073 --> 01:11:28,847
He did.

465
01:11:35,773 --> 01:11:37,349
And who is this?

466
01:11:37,440 --> 01:11:39,597
Isildur's heir?

467
01:11:39,732 --> 01:11:42,771
It takes more to make a king
than a broken Elvish blade.

468
01:11:47,493 --> 01:11:50,095
I guess that concludes negotiations.

469
01:11:52,233 --> 01:11:53,430
I do not believe it.

470
01:11:55,410 --> 01:11:56,815
I will not.

471
01:12:07,968 --> 01:12:09,967
[Black Speech] <i> Ash nazg durb! </i>
[English]  One Ring to rule!

472
01:12:12,859 --> 01:12:14,691
Pull back.

473
01:12:14,943 --> 01:12:17,023
Pull back!

474
01:12:19,159 --> 01:12:21,157
[Black Speech] <i> Ash nazg durb! </i>
[English]  One Ring to rule!

475
01:12:29,215 --> 01:12:31,274
It's gone, Mr. Frodo.

476
01:12:33,174 --> 01:12:36,717
The light's passed on, away towards the north.

477
01:12:36,821 --> 01:12:38,735
Something's drawn its gaze.

478
01:12:53,255 --> 01:12:55,254
[Black Speech] <i> Ash nazg durb! </i>
[English]  One Ring to rule!

479
01:12:56,197 --> 01:12:58,988
Hold your ground! Hold your ground.

480
01:13:00,833 --> 01:13:05,067
Sons of Gondor, of Rohan, my brothers!

481
01:13:07,866 --> 01:13:09,821
I see in your eyes...

482
01:13:10,158 --> 01:13:14,239
the same fear that would take the heart of me.

483
01:13:16,199 --> 01:13:19,950
A day may come when the courage of Men fails...

484
01:13:19,971 --> 01:13:23,566
when we forsake our friends and
break all bonds of fellowship.

485
01:13:23,596 --> 01:13:26,409
But it is not this day.

486
01:13:26,668 --> 01:13:29,734
An hour of wolves and shattered shields...

487
01:13:29,899 --> 01:13:32,777
when the age of Men comes crashing down.

488
01:13:32,919 --> 01:13:35,404
But it is not this day.

489
01:13:35,576 --> 01:13:37,235
This day we fight!

490
01:13:39,327 --> 01:13:43,363
By all that you hold dear on this good earth...

491
01:13:43,535 --> 01:13:47,778
I bid you stand, Men of the West!

492
01:15:16,160 --> 01:15:19,702
Never thought I'd die fighting
side by side with an Elf.

493
01:15:20,170 --> 01:15:22,493
What about side by side with a friend?

494
01:15:26,004 --> 01:15:27,787
Aye.

495
01:15:28,609 --> 01:15:30,419
I could do that.

496
01:16:00,695 --> 01:16:02,790
Do you remember the Shire, Mr. Frodo?

497
01:16:05,747 --> 01:16:07,999
It'll be spring soon.

498
01:16:08,768 --> 01:16:11,502
And the orchards will be in blossom.

499
01:16:11,634 --> 01:16:15,337
And the birds will be nesting in the hazel thicket.

500
01:16:16,687 --> 01:16:20,712
And they'll be sowing the summer
barley in the lower fields...

501
01:16:21,739 --> 01:16:26,133
and eating the first of the strawberries with cream.

502
01:16:28,041 --> 01:16:30,540
Do you remember the taste of strawberries?

503
01:16:32,104 --> 01:16:33,843
No, Sam.

504
01:16:33,980 --> 01:16:36,962
I can't recall the taste of food...

505
01:16:38,094 --> 01:16:41,377
nor the sound of water...

506
01:16:41,532 --> 01:16:45,132
nor the touch of grass.

507
01:16:46,064 --> 01:16:47,636
I'm...

508
01:16:48,513 --> 01:16:49,887
naked in the dark.

509
01:16:51,533 --> 01:16:53,840
There's... there's nothing.

510
01:16:53,981 --> 01:16:58,717
No veil between me and the wheel of fire.

511
01:16:59,971 --> 01:17:01,879
I can see him...

512
01:17:02,264 --> 01:17:03,964
with my waking eyes.

513
01:17:04,972 --> 01:17:07,466
Then let us be rid of it...

514
01:17:08,045 --> 01:17:10,295
once and for all.

515
01:17:11,015 --> 01:17:13,089
Come on, Mr. Frodo.

516
01:17:13,254 --> 01:17:15,884
I can't carry it for you...

517
01:17:16,275 --> 01:17:18,345
but I can carry you.

518
01:17:18,880 --> 01:17:20,633
Come on!

519
01:17:51,019 --> 01:17:53,970
Aragorn.

520
01:18:05,499 --> 01:18:09,249
Elessar.

521
01:18:20,085 --> 01:18:22,510
For Frodo.

522
01:18:57,431 --> 01:18:58,935
Look, Mr. Frodo.

523
01:18:59,619 --> 01:19:01,855
A doorway.

524
01:19:02,432 --> 01:19:04,101
We're almost there.

525
01:19:06,442 --> 01:19:10,389
Clever Hobbits to climb so high!

526
01:19:24,308 --> 01:19:25,978
Mustn't go that way.

527
01:19:27,486 --> 01:19:29,982
Mustn't hurt the precious.

528
01:19:30,143 --> 01:19:31,895
You swore!

529
01:19:32,070 --> 01:19:34,144
You swore on the precious!

530
01:19:36,028 --> 01:19:37,984
Smeagol promised!

531
01:19:38,894 --> 01:19:40,895
Smeagol lied.

532
01:20:33,327 --> 01:20:35,240
Frodo!

533
01:21:02,288 --> 01:21:04,072
Eagles.

534
01:21:05,464 --> 01:21:06,988
The eagles are coming!

535
01:21:29,791 --> 01:21:31,662
Frodo!

536
01:21:36,874 --> 01:21:38,195
I'm here, Sam.

537
01:21:45,626 --> 01:21:47,291
Destroy it!

538
01:21:57,814 --> 01:22:01,117
Go on! Now!

539
01:22:01,252 --> 01:22:03,828
Throw it in the fire!

540
01:22:17,191 --> 01:22:19,878
What are you waiting for?

541
01:22:21,723 --> 01:22:24,124
Just let it go!

542
01:22:57,299 --> 01:22:59,539
The Ring is mine.

543
01:23:03,080 --> 01:23:04,833
No.

544
01:23:05,216 --> 01:23:06,537
No.

545
01:23:14,957 --> 01:23:17,634
No!

546
01:25:01,947 --> 01:25:03,850
Yes!

547
01:25:05,020 --> 01:25:06,726
Yes!

548
01:25:07,833 --> 01:25:10,722
Precious! Precious!

549
01:25:10,855 --> 01:25:14,060
Precious! Precious!

550
01:26:06,901 --> 01:26:08,769
Give me your hand!

551
01:26:17,110 --> 01:26:19,516
Take my hand!

552
01:26:22,163 --> 01:26:23,522
No!

553
01:26:30,758 --> 01:26:32,733
Don't you let go.

554
01:26:37,320 --> 01:26:38,897
Don't let go.

555
01:26:40,499 --> 01:26:41,988
Reach!

556
01:28:11,080 --> 01:28:13,948
Frodo!

557
01:28:14,518 --> 01:28:17,537
Frodo!

558
01:29:38,797 --> 01:29:40,665
It's gone.

559
01:29:45,099 --> 01:29:46,873
It's done.

560
01:29:47,339 --> 01:29:49,373
Yes, Mr. Frodo.

561
01:29:50,726 --> 01:29:53,163
It's over now.

562
01:30:18,801 --> 01:30:21,171
I can see the Shire.

563
01:30:23,385 --> 01:30:25,708
The Brandywine River.

564
01:30:27,813 --> 01:30:29,834
Bag End.

565
01:30:32,136 --> 01:30:34,880
Gandalf's fireworks.

566
01:30:35,262 --> 01:30:39,048
The lights in the Party Tree.

567
01:30:40,522 --> 01:30:43,670
Rosie Cotton dancing.

568
01:30:44,793 --> 01:30:47,506
She had ribbons in her hair.

569
01:30:50,419 --> 01:30:53,381
If ever I was to marry someone...

570
01:30:54,274 --> 01:30:56,545
it would've been her.

571
01:30:57,971 --> 01:31:00,045
It would've been her.

572
01:31:12,140 --> 01:31:15,387
I'm glad to be with you, Samwise Gamgee...

573
01:31:19,641 --> 01:31:22,597
here at the end of all things.

574
01:33:12,151 --> 01:33:14,231
Gandalf?

575
01:33:33,821 --> 01:33:35,853
Frodo!

576
01:33:55,593 --> 01:33:57,440
Gimli!

577
01:35:40,291 --> 01:35:44,078
Now come the days of the king.

578
01:35:49,043 --> 01:35:51,407
May they be blessed.

579
01:36:11,649 --> 01:36:14,337
This day does not belong to one man...

580
01:36:14,462 --> 01:36:16,376
but to all.

581
01:36:18,004 --> 01:36:20,960
Let us together rebuild this world...

582
01:36:21,129 --> 01:36:25,372
that we may share in the days of peace.

583
01:37:19,843 --> 01:37:21,341
[Sindarin] <i>Hannon le.</i>
[English] Thank you.

584
01:38:59,687 --> 01:39:01,803
My friends...

585
01:39:07,083 --> 01:39:09,770
you bow to no one.

586
01:39:53,859 --> 01:39:56,021
And thus it was.

587
01:39:56,151 --> 01:39:59,807
A Fourth Age of Middle-earth began.

588
01:39:59,953 --> 01:40:02,521
And the Fellowship of the Ring...

589
01:40:02,662 --> 01:40:07,185
though eternally bound by friendship and love...

590
01:40:07,349 --> 01:40:09,765
was ended.

591
01:40:14,747 --> 01:40:19,566
Thirteen months to the day since
Gandalf sent us on our long journey...

592
01:40:19,694 --> 01:40:23,943
we found ourselves looking upon a familiar sight.

593
01:40:26,466 --> 01:40:29,189
We were home.

594
01:40:35,738 --> 01:40:37,609
Hi.

595
01:40:54,750 --> 01:40:56,986
Hey, watch the pumpkin.

596
01:41:45,016 --> 01:41:46,613
More of the same, Rosie.

597
01:41:46,787 --> 01:41:48,777
Good night, lads.

598
01:42:46,272 --> 01:42:50,287
How do you pick up the threads of an old life?

599
01:42:51,585 --> 01:42:53,831
How do you go on...

600
01:42:53,981 --> 01:42:59,204
when in your heart you begin to understand...

601
01:43:00,440 --> 01:43:03,411
there is no going back?

602
01:43:04,086 --> 01:43:07,790
There are some things that time cannot mend...

603
01:43:08,253 --> 01:43:11,210
some hurts that go too deep...

604
01:43:12,941 --> 01:43:15,795
that have taken hold.

605
01:43:53,882 --> 01:43:55,797
Mr. Frodo?

606
01:43:59,092 --> 01:44:00,508
What is it?

607
01:44:02,320 --> 01:44:06,288
It's been four years to the day since Weathertop, Sam.

608
01:44:06,957 --> 01:44:09,669
It's never really healed.

609
01:44:13,624 --> 01:44:18,885
"There and Back Again." A
Hobbit's tale by Bilbo Baggins.

610
01:44:19,562 --> 01:44:23,417
And "The Lord of the Rings" by Frodo Baggins.

611
01:44:23,886 --> 01:44:26,084
You finished it.

612
01:44:28,939 --> 01:44:30,463
Not quite.

613
01:44:31,231 --> 01:44:33,839
There's room for a little more.

614
01:44:36,439 --> 01:44:40,678
Bilbo once told me his part in this tale would end...

615
01:44:40,814 --> 01:44:44,128
that each of us must come and go in the telling.

616
01:44:44,982 --> 01:44:47,844
Bilbo's story was now over.

617
01:44:48,315 --> 01:44:51,261
There would be no more journeys for him...

618
01:44:51,389 --> 01:44:52,970
save one.

619
01:44:53,681 --> 01:44:57,327
Tell me again, lad, where are we going?

620
01:44:57,431 --> 01:44:59,463
To the harbor, Bilbo.

621
01:44:59,619 --> 01:45:02,341
The Elves have accorded you a special honor...

622
01:45:02,483 --> 01:45:05,133
a place on the last ship to leave Middle-earth.

623
01:45:06,806 --> 01:45:08,507
Frodo...

624
01:45:09,932 --> 01:45:14,471
any chance of seeing that old Ring of mine again?

625
01:45:15,089 --> 01:45:17,339
The one I gave you.

626
01:45:20,975 --> 01:45:23,131
I'm sorry, Uncle.

627
01:45:25,663 --> 01:45:28,303
I'm afraid I lost it.

628
01:45:28,475 --> 01:45:30,266
Oh.

629
01:45:30,819 --> 01:45:32,349
Pity.

630
01:45:35,090 --> 01:45:38,965
I should like to have held it one last time.

631
01:46:08,062 --> 01:46:13,141
Well, here's a sight I have never seen before.

632
01:46:27,284 --> 01:46:30,645
The power of the Three Rings is ended.

633
01:46:31,397 --> 01:46:34,224
The time has come...

634
01:46:34,367 --> 01:46:37,649
for the dominion of Men.

635
01:46:38,090 --> 01:46:41,088
[Sindarin] <i>I Aear cân ven na mar.</i>
[English] The sea calls us to home.

636
01:46:50,045 --> 01:46:52,224
I think I'm...

637
01:46:52,390 --> 01:46:56,774
quite ready for another adventure.

638
01:47:27,811 --> 01:47:30,107
Farewell...

639
01:47:30,258 --> 01:47:33,029
my brave Hobbits.

640
01:47:34,946 --> 01:47:36,978
My work is now finished.

641
01:47:40,780 --> 01:47:45,776
Here at last, on the shores of the sea...

642
01:47:46,406 --> 01:47:49,280
comes the end of our Fellowship.

643
01:47:52,812 --> 01:47:55,312
I will not say, "Do not weep"...

644
01:47:55,990 --> 01:47:59,984
for not all tears are an evil.

645
01:48:17,502 --> 01:48:19,441
It is time, Frodo.

646
01:48:24,951 --> 01:48:26,984
What does he mean?

647
01:48:29,431 --> 01:48:32,319
We set out to save the Shire, Sam.

648
01:48:33,910 --> 01:48:36,660
And it has been saved.

649
01:48:40,318 --> 01:48:42,995
But not for me.

650
01:48:43,911 --> 01:48:46,365
You don't mean that.

651
01:48:47,557 --> 01:48:49,652
You can't leave.

652
01:48:58,080 --> 01:49:00,823
The last pages are for you, Sam.

653
01:52:33,726 --> 01:52:36,594
My dear Sam

654
01:52:38,519 --> 01:52:41,848
You cannot always be torn in two.

655
01:52:42,008 --> 01:52:46,143
You will have to be one and whole for many years.

656
01:52:46,748 --> 01:52:52,346
You have so much to enjoy and to be and to do.

657
01:52:53,468 --> 01:52:56,766
Your part in the story will go on.

658
01:52:57,478 --> 01:52:59,262
Well...

659
01:53:01,125 --> 01:53:02,852
I'm back.

660
01:59:00,149 --> 01:59:05,599
...into the west.

